    "result_text": "The full build succeeds with all tests green. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and all 3 email tests pass, along with everything else.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional owner `email` support so that, when present, it must be a syntactically valid address, is stored/returned lower-cased, and is rejected with 400 when invalid.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `email` property to the `OwnerFields` schema with `format: email`. Because the generator runs with `performBeanValidation=true`, this emits `@Email` on the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`, so an invalid address (e.g. `not-an-email`) is rejected as a 400 via the existing Bean Validation \u2192 `ExceptionControllerAdvice` path. It's not in `required`, so a missing email is accepted.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added an `email` column (`@Column`, `@Email`) with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it between the DTO and entity by name.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added a `normalizeEmail` helper (lower-cases via `Locale.ROOT`, passes through `null`) and applied it in both `addOwner` and `updateOwner`, mirroring the existing telephone-normalization pattern.\n\n4. **Schema/data SQL** \u2014 Added the `email` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres). The tests run on the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to exist in `schema.sql`. I also gave the positional `owners` seed inserts in the hsqldb and mysql `data.sql` files explicit column lists (`(id, first_name, last_name, address, city, telephone)`) so they remain valid now that the table has an extra column (h2 and postgres already used column lists).\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreLowercasesEmail`, `errorRejectsInvalidEmail`, and `functionalityAcceptsMissingEmail` all pass, and `BUILD SUCCESS` overall.",
